  "mechanism": {
    "admission": "Only unanchored Present with the existing can_reuse_acquisition geometry.",
    "float": "Complete initial traversal, validation and terminal control before useful-read credit. Reuse its membership and progress without another consuming traversal.",
    "histograms": "If populated acquisition allocated histogram storage, perform the consuming pass. Use its entire Acquisition, including populated and progress; changing replay data can alter membership. Stale allocated history keeps this path.",
    "publication": "The existing FoldStep finalizer owns the result and sample lease. Global absence still examines all selected series.",
    "fallback": "Unproven geometry, anchors, statistics projection, buffering, derived/no-matrix and other fold kinds retain their paths.",
    "sharing": "Both Present no-op callbacks use ignore_sample<StorageError> directly, without a function pointer. Existing acquire continues using that item. No new state, history buffers, allocation, ABI, arithmetic or limit change."
  },
